[size=5][b][color=#E8C88A]Health Regen - Configurable[/color][/b][/size]

Human and vampire health regeneration in one configurable mod. Choose separate rates for each form, keep regeneration outside combat, or allow it during combat. Both forms default to 1.5% per second.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Stops healing at the limit[/color][/b][/size]

Regeneration stops when your health bar or current vampire segment is full. This avoids the original vampire mod's repeated healing attempts at the limit.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]

Required: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Mod Setting Menu 1.0.6 or later[/url]. Open Mod Settings and press Apply to save and update gameplay.

[size=3][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual configuration (without the menu)[/color][/b][/size]

Load a save once to create settings.ini, then close the game. Open this file inside your The Blood of Dawnwalker game folder:
[code]Dawnwalker\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods\HealthRegeneration\settings.ini[/code]
The default settings are:
[code][Settings]
vampireRegenPercent = 1.5
humanRegenPercent = 1.5
combatRegen = 0
restoreVampireSegments = 0
debugLogging = 0[/code]
Change either regeneration rate using the steps above; 1.5 means 1.5% per second. For combatRegen, restoreVampireSegments and debugLogging, use 0 for Off or 1 for On. Save the file, restart the game and load a save to apply your changes.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vortex:[/color][/b] Install Health-Regen-Configurable.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual:[/color][/b] Copy the archive's Dawnwalker folder into ...\steamapps\common\The Blood of Dawnwalker\, preserving the folder structure.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Credits and source[/color][/b][/size]

